1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,266
Sixty-two percent of people earning six

2
00:00:02,266 --> 00:00:04,589
figures still live paycheck to paycheck.

3
00:00:04,589 --> 00:00:07,610
And a two-hundred-fifty-year-old story explains why.

4
00:00:07,610 --> 00:00:08,277
In 1765,

5
00:00:08,277 --> 00:00:11,446
philosopher Denis Diderot was gifted a

6
00:00:11,446 --> 00:00:13,364
luxurious scarlet robe.

7
00:00:13,364 --> 00:00:14,865
Next to that robe,

8
00:00:14,865 --> 00:00:17,616
his old wooden desk looked cheap.

9
00:00:17,616 --> 00:00:19,618
So he replaced the desk.

10
00:00:19,618 --> 00:00:20,702
Then the rug.

11
00:00:20,702 --> 00:00:23,120
Then every chair in his home.

12
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:26,085
Psychologists call this the Diderot Effect.

13
00:00:26,085 --> 00:00:28,499
You rarely buy just one upgrade—you

14
00:00:28,499 --> 00:00:30,499
buy a whole new identity that

15
00:00:30,499 --> 00:00:33,050
demands five more purchases to match.

16
00:00:33,050 --> 00:00:34,376
To break the spiral,

17
00:00:34,376 --> 00:00:36,299
use the Invisible Raise Rule:

18
00:00:36,299 --> 00:00:38,089
whenever your income jumps,

19
00:00:38,089 --> 00:00:41,072
automatically route fifty percent into assets

20
00:00:41,072 --> 00:00:43,260
before it ever hits your checking

21
00:00:43,260 --> 00:00:43,790
account.

22
00:00:43,790 --> 00:00:46,356
Real wealth isn't what people see

23
00:00:46,356 --> 00:00:49,232
in your driveway—it's the freedom you

24
00:00:49,232 --> 00:00:50,632
didn't trade away.

25
00:00:50,632 --> 00:00:52,420
Which is exactly why...
